<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Achieng translated triangle PQR by the vector <m>\mathbf{T} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -4 \\ 5 \end{array}\right)}</m>. The vertices are <m>P({1},\,{-4})</m>, <m>Q({4},\,{-4})</m> and <m>R({1},\,{-2})</m>. She wrote the images as <m>P'({6},\,{-8})</m>, <m>Q'({0},\,{1})</m> and <m>R'({-3},\,{3})</m>. One of her images is wrong.</p><p>(a) Which image is wrong?</p><div>[ None: all three are right | P' | Q' | R' ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct coordinates of that image.</p><div>( <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> )  </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Add <m>\mathbf{T}</m> to every vertex and compare with Achieng's points.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Vertex</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Coordinates</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Vertex + T</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Achieng's image</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"/></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">P</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({1},\,{-4})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({-3},\,{1})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({6},\,{-8})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">wrong</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Q</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({4},\,{-4})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({0},\,{1})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({0},\,{1})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">right</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">R</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({1},\,{-2})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({-3},\,{3})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>({-3},\,{3})</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">right</cell></row></tabular><p>(a) P' is wrong. She swapped the two components of <m>\mathbf{T}</m> at that vertex.</p><p>(b) The correct image is <m>({-3},\,{1})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>P'</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-3</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>